<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eastern Depot</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1420">1420</a>–<a href="/years/1644">1644</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Eastern Bureau, Dongchang</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Eastern Depot was a spy and secret police agency of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming dynasty</a> run by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eunuch">eunuchs</a>, created in 1420 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yongle-emperor">Yongle Emperor</a>, who had usurped the throne from his nephew in 1402, to suppress political opposition. Named for its place east of the imperial palace, it spied on officials of every rank, military officers, scholars, rebels and the general populace, and handed those it arrested to the Jinyiwei for interrogation. In the late Ming it had its own forces and prisons and grew so powerful that even officials were ordered to kowtow to its leaders. It lasted until the end of the dynasty in 1644; its chiefs included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-zhen-eunuch">Wang Zhen</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-jin">Liu Jin</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wei-zhongxian">Wei Zhongxian</a>.</p></div>
